{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For.</b> All this is on account of the child who will be born to us, and we know that when Sennacherib came, Hezekiah was thirty-nine years old, therefore he called him a child at the time of the prophet's prophecy. Some say that פלא יועץ אל גבור אבי עד are names of the Name, and the name of the child is שר שלום. But the correct view in my eyes is that all these are names of the child: פלא, because HaShem performed a wonder in his days; יועץ, for so was Hezekiah, and 'the king's counselor' (2 Chronicles 30:2); אל גבור, because he was mighty; אבי עד, because the kingdom of the house of David endured on his account, and עד is like 'who dwells forever' (Isaiah 57:15); שר שלום, because there was peace in his days, and so it is written (2 Chronicles 32:22):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:00.889079956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}